0,Nilotic languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nilotic_languages,"The Nilotic languages are languages spoken across wide areas between Egypt, Ethiopia, Sudan, South Sudan, Democratic Republic of Congo, Kenya, Uganda and Tanzania by the Nilotic peoples.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
1,"Dinka, Southwestern | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/dik/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..sYl2WHRTkpu4OU3oz-MYO6HL2HyLEOhCjL1u4A_mGl0,Southwestern Dinka is a stable indigenous language of South Sudan. It belongs to the Nilo-Saharan language family and is part of the Dinka macrolanguage. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.,"Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
2,Southwestern Dinka - dik (Nilo-Saharan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/dik/,"People Groups who primarily speak Southwestern Dinka. To download a comprehensive people group list in spreadsheet form, visit our Research Data page.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
3,"Dinka, Southwestern in South Sudan people group... | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/15363/OD,"The Southwestern Dinka speak Dinka, Southwestern, a Nilotic language within the Eastern Sudanic branch of the Nilo-Saharan family. This language is indigenous to South Sudan and is used as a first language by all members of the ethnic group.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
4,Southwestern Dinka Translator | Polytranslator,https://www.polytranslator.com/southwestern-dinka/,"Southwestern Dinka, also known as Rek, is spoken by around 1 million people in South Sudan. It is one of the dialects of the Dinka language, which belongs to the Nilotic branch of the Nilo-Saharan language family.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
5,Southwestern Dinka Language New... - Bible in My Language,https://www.bibleinmylanguage.com/southwestern-dinka-language-new-testament-lek-yam-dik-south-sudan/,"The Southwestern Dinka Language New Testament, known as Lëk yam, is a vital resource for the Dinka-speaking community of South Sudan.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
6,"Dinka, Southwestern | Accent Network",https://accentnetwork.com/dinka-southwestern/,"Nilo-Saharan. Dinka, Southwestern, Sudan.Dinka, spoken by approximately 2 million in South Sudan, part of the Nilotic family. Market Insights. Content includes radio and storytelling, with digital media growing among youth.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
7,Dinka: Have You Heard Of This Interesting... - Crystal Clear Translation,https://crystalcleartranslation.com/dinka-have-you-heard-of-this-interesting-western-nilotic-language/,"Part of the Nilo-Saharan language family, Dinka, also known as Jieng, is a Western Nilotic language spoken primarily by the Dinka people. In total, there are 1.35 million speakers of the Dinka language, primarily in South Sudan.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
8,Comparing Nilo-Saharan East Africans And West Africans... | MedShun,https://medshun.com/article/are-nilo-saharan-east-africans-or-west-africans,"Some examples of Nilo-Saharan ethnic groups found in East Africa include the Dinka, Nuer, Shilluk, Maasai, Kalenjin, and Luo. These groups have distinct cultural practices, languages, and traditions that are unique to their respective communities.","Dinka, Southwestern",Nilo-Saharan
